Emacsvox
********

Welcome to the Emacsvox user manual.  Begin with the introduction,
follow the installation path until Emacsvox speaks, and then try the
Guided Tutorial for step-by-step practice or Basic Usage for a concise
first session.  Platform and compatibility detail is available in Speech
Backends when you need it.  Exact commands, options, and keymaps are in
the separate *note Emacsvox Reference Manual: (emacsvox-reference)Top.
Selected historical Emacspeak material is in the separate *note
Emacspeak Heritage: (emacsvox-heritage)Top. manual and is not current
setup guidance.  For rapidly evolving development and Aural Presentation
rule-authoring details, also consult ‘README.org’ and
‘etc/aural-presentation-reference.org’ in the source tree.

   The manual is divided into the following chapters:

* Menu:

